{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LEet9eHBjcAM1t7Ln6HvUx","type":"tool_result","content":"total 200\ndrwxr-xr-x.  2 scheschb amazon   150 Sep  2 13:04 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 50 scheschb amazon 16384 Sep  2 13:05 ..\n-rw-r--r--.  1 scheschb amazon  1406 Sep  2 13:04 combined.log\n-rwxr-xr-x.  1 scheschb amazon 68784 Sep  2 13:04 libcsphincs_all.so\n-rwxr-xr-x.  1 scheschb amazon 49792 Sep  2 13:04 libsha2.so\n-rwxr-xr-x.  1 scheschb amazon 26536 Sep  2 13:04 libsphincs_core.so\n-rwxr-xr-x.  1 scheschb amazon 31184 Sep  2 13:04 libsphincs_core_det.so\n#!/bin/bash\n# Builds the C reference implementation as shared libraries for every valid\n# CMake cache-variable combination (HASH_BACKEND x THASH x SECPAR).\n#\n# Output layout:  cbuild/<backend>-<thash>-<secpar>/lib{sphincs_core_det,<backend>}.so\n#\n# OpenSSL comes from the nix store because the distro's -devel headers are\n# absent in this environment; the linked libcrypto is functionally identical.\nset -u\n\nROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nSRC=\"$ROOT/c_src\"\nOUT=\"$ROOT/cbuild\"\n\nSSL_INC=$(ls -d /nix/store/*-openssl-*-dev/include 2>/dev/null | head -1)\n# Link against the *system* libcrypto: the nix-store one is built against a\n# newer glibc than this host provides, so a .so linked to it cannot be dlopen'd.\nSSL_SO=$(ls /usr/lib64/libcrypto.so.3 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcrypto.so.3 2>/dev/null | head -1)\n\nmkdir -p \"$OUT\"\n--- negative control (C 192f vs Rust 256f-built lib, N=24 params) ---\nDIFF hash_message.digest idx=0 len=33\n  first byte 30: C=33 R=22\nDIFF hash_message.tree ml=0 C=3264851243450821548 R=14562304273093864\nDIFF hash_message.leaf ml=0 C=1 R=96\nDIFF hash_message.digest idx=1 len=33\n  first byte 30: C=33 R=22\nDIFF hash_message.tree ml=1 C=8224590120907020538 R=14571659866643747\nDIFF hash_message.leaf ml=1 C=5 R=473\nDIFF hash_message.digest idx=2 len=33\n  first byte 30: C=d5 R=22","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_b