{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a52ad26355bd92fdf","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TVfXZwqjfFGjnaaEeLdMeZ","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-asBfB4/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-JZe0gx/ea246c20-3a08-49a0-aeed-8ef41fe5c703/tasks/a52ad26355bd92fdf.output","summary":"## Verification method\n\nI read all ten C sources + all headers against the twelve Rust files, and then built a scratch `dlopen`-based differential probe (kept in `$TMPDIR`, nothing added to the repo) that drives the exported symbols of `cbuild/<combo>/libcsphincs_all.so` vs `rbuild/<combo>/libsphincs_core_det.so` with adversarial inputs. Existing suites also still pass (`configs` 36/36, `errors` 27/27 for `sha2,robust,128s`).\n\n## Findings\n\n**1. `wots_gen_leafx1`: `info->wots_steps == NULL` — C crashes, Rust silently substitutes zeros**\n- C: `c_src/app/src/wotsx1.c:41` — `uint32_t wots_k = info->wots_steps[i] | wots_k_mask;` unconditionally dereferences the pointer.\n- Rust: `translation/src/wotsx1.rs:151-154` — `with_leaf_info` does `if !ci.wots_steps.is_null() { copy_nonoverlapping(...) }`, leaving a zero `[u32; SPX_WOTS_LEN]` otherwise; `wotsx1.rs:176` also skips the copy-back.\n- Confirmed empirically (`sha2-robust-128s`): `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1` with `wots_steps=NULL` → C `SIGSEGV`, Rust returns `dest=bb85b57fd13b19ffc8d0518658698d29`. Same for `SPX_wots_treehashx1` (`tree_height=2`): C `SIGSEGV`, Rust returns `root=ab63b7236b7772d213fab811dd1c0e42`.\n\n**2. `wots_gen_leafx1`: `info->wots_sig == NULL` with `leaf_idx == wots_sign_leaf` — C crashes, Rust silently skips the store**\n- C: `c_src/app/src/wotsx1.c:57-59` — `if (k == wots_k) memcpy(info->wots_sig + i * SPX_N, buffer, SPX_N);`. With `wots_k_mask == 0` (i.e. `leaf_idx == info->wots_sign_leaf`) `wots_k` is in `0..15`, so the `memcpy` *does* run and dereferences NULL.\n- Rust: `translation/src/wotsx1.rs:86-91` — `if let Some(sig) = info.wots_sig.as_deref_mut()` makes the whole store a no-op; `wotsx1.rs:156-160` maps a NULL pointer to `None`.\n- Confirmed: C `SIGSEGV`, Rust completes normally.\n\n**3. `seedexpander`: `ctx->buffer_pos > 16` — C succeeds (reads adjacent struct bytes), Rust panics/aborts**\n- C: `c_src/app/src/rng.c:75-85`. `16 - ctx->buffer_pos` is `unsigned long`, so for `buffer_pos = 20` it wraps to `2^64-4`; the `xlen <= avail` branch is taken and `memcpy(x+offset, ctx->buffer + 20, xlen)` reads the first bytes of the `buffer_pos` field. Returns `RNG_SUCCESS`.\n- Rust: `translation/src/rng.rs:176` reproduces the wrapping arithmetic correctly (`16u64.wrapping_sub(ctx.buffer_pos)`), but the subsequent slice index at `rng.rs:183` (`&ctx.buffer[bp..bp + n]`) is bounds-checked. Same problem at `rng.rs:191-194` on the multi-block path.\n- Confirmed: with `buffer_pos=20, length_remaining=1000, xlen=4` → C `ret=0 bp=24 lr=996 x=0000000000000000`; Rust `panicked at src/rng.rs:183:56: range start index 20 out of range for slice of length 16` → `Aborted` (the release profile sets `panic = \"abort\"`, so this kills the process rather than returning an error).\n\n**4. `SPX_compute_root` wrapper: `tree_height == 0` — the `from_raw_parts` length is too small**\n- C: `c_src/app/src/utils.c:70` — `for (i = 0; i < tree_height - 1; i++)` with `uint32_t tree_height == 0` gives `0xFFFFFFFF` iterations. C first *successfully* reads `auth_path[0..SPX_N]` (utils.c:62/66), mutates `addr` via `set_tree_height`/`set_tree_index` and hashes for a long while before running off the end.\n- Rust: `translation/src/utils.rs:241` — `let ap_len = (tree_height as usize).saturating_mul(SPX_N);` is `0` for `tree_height == 0`, so `utils.rs:60`/`utils.rs:63` panic on the very first `&auth_path[0..SPX_N]`, before any hashing or any mutation of `addr`.\n- Confirmed: Rust `panicked at src/utils.rs:63:60: range end index 16 out of range for slice of length 0` → `Aborted`; C runs and eventually `SIGSEGV`s. Both die, but at different points and with different observable side effects on `addr`. (The loop-bound wrapping itself is correct — `utils.rs:68` uses `wrapping_sub(1)`.)\n\n**5. `randombytes.c` (`/dev/urandom` variant): failed `read()` handled differently**\n- C: `c_src/app/src/randombytes.c:34-41` — `i = (unsigned long long)read(fd, x, i);` turns `-1` into `0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF`, which passes `i < 1`, so C then does `x += i; xlen -= i` (wild pointer).\n- Rust: `translation/src/randombytes.rs:66-72` maps `Err(_)` onto the `sleep(1); continue;` retry path.\n- This is documented in the Rust comment and is not reachable via the ABI (see below), so it is low-impact; noted for completeness.\n\n**6. `SPX_treehash` with a NULL `gen_leaf` — different crash mode**\n- C: `c_src/app/src/utils.c:121` calls through the function pointer (SIGSEGV).\n- Rust: `translation/src/utils.rs:269` — `gen_leaf.expect(\"treehash: NULL gen_leaf callback\")` panics → abort. Both crash; only the mode/message differs.\n\n**7. Latent (not observed): `memmove` → non-overlapping copy in `sign.rs`**\n- C uses `memmove` at `c_src/app/src/sign.c:254` and `sign.c:284` precisely because `m` and `sm` may overlap.\n- Rust `translation/src/sign.rs:319` and `sign.rs:357` use `copy_from_slice` (i.e. `copy_nonoverlapping`) over slices that would alias, and the wrappers `sign.rs:457-458` / `sign.rs:478-479` build overlapping `&mut`/`&` slices from the same memory (UB).\n- I tested the realistic in-place case (`crypto_sign_open(sm, &mlen, sm, smlen, pk)` with `mlen = 20000 > SPX_BYTES`, so the regions genuinely overlap) and C and Rust produced byte-identical results, so this is a formal/latent issue rather than a reproduced divergence.\n\n## Explicitly verified as *matching* (no divergence)\n\n- **`from_raw_parts`/`from_raw_parts_mut` lengths**: every wrapper checked against the bytes C actually touches — `SPX_compute_root` (`root`=N, `leaf`=N, `auth_path`=`tree_height*N`, exact for `tree_height>=1`), `SPX_treehash` (`auth_path`=`(tree_height+1)*N`, which is deliberately the true C extent — C *does* write the extra block for out-of-range `leaf_idx`; I reproduced this and both wrote the same bytes at offset `4*N`), `SPX_wots_treehashx1`/`SPX_fors_treehashx1` (`tree_height*N`), `SPX_merkle_sign` (`SPX_WOTS_BYTES + SPX_TREE_HEIGHT*SPX_N`), `SPX_fors_sign`/`SPX_fors_pk_from_sig` (`SPX_FORS_BYTES` / `SPX_FORS_MSG_BYTES` / `SPX_N`), `SPX_wots_pk_from_sig` (`SPX_WOTS_LEN*SPX_N`), `SPX_chain_lengths` (`SPX_WOTS_LEN` words / `SPX_N`), `crypto_sign*` (`SPX_BYTES`, `SPX_BYTES+mlen`, `smlen`, `CRYPTO_*BYTES`), all `rng` entry points (32/8/48/16 and `xlen`). Only #4 above is wrong.\n- **Integer types**: `unsigned long` → `u64` (`seedexpander{,_init}`, `AES_XOF_struct.buffer_pos`/`length_remaining`), `unsigned long long` → `u64` (`randombytes`, `crypto_sign{,_open}`, `crypto_sign_*bytes`), `size_t` → `usize` (`crypto_sign_signature`/`_verify`), `unsigned int` → `c_uint` (`ull_to_bytes`/`bytes_to_ull` lengths), `unsigned *` → `*mut u32`. `AES_XOF_struct` (80 B), `AES256_CTR_DRBG_struct` (52 B) and `spx_ctx` layouts all agree for all 48 configs.\n- **`sign.c:151/230` `idx_leaf = (tree & ((1 << SPX_TREE_HEIGHT)-1))`**: not reachable. `SPX_TREE_HEIGHT = SPX_FULL_HEIGHT/SPX_D` is 9 (128s/192s), 3 (128f/192f), 8 (256s), 4 (256f) — always ≤ 9, so C's `int` `1 <<` and Rust's `1u64 <<` (`sign.rs:187/298`) agree.\n- **thash aliasing / staging**: all six `out == in` sites stage through a temporary at the correct point — `utils.rs:78-79` and `:83-84` (`thash(buffer+SPX_N, buffer, 2)` / `thash(buffer, buffer, 2)`), `utils.rs:156-158` (`treehash`), `utilsx1.rs:102-103` (`thash(&current[N], &current[0], 2)`, staged *after* the left node is copied in from the stack), `wots.rs:36-38` (`gen_chain`), `wotsx1.rs:102-110`, `fors.rs:51-53`. I also confirmed the C `thash` (robust and simple, all backends) fully consumes `in` into `buf` before writing `out`, so the temporary is behaviourally identical.\n- **Other wrapping arithmetic**: `max_idx = (uint32_t)((1<<tree_height)-1)` → `1u32.wrapping_shl(h).wrapping_sub(1)`; `(uint32_t)(1<<tree_height)` → `wrapping_shl`; `i*(1<<SPX_FORS_HEIGHT)` → `wrapping_mul`; `start+steps` in `gen_chain` → `wrapping_add`; `SPX_WOTS_W-1-msg_base_w[i]` → `wrapping_sub` chain; `base_w`'s `int` promotion of `total`.\n- **`rng.c` ordering**: the `x == NULL` check strictly precedes the `xlen >= length_remaining` check in both (`rng.rs:387` then `rng.rs:167`); confirmed `se(NULL, 1000) == -2` in both. `seedexpander_init` maxlen boundary (`0xFFFFFFFF` → 0, `0x100000000` → -1), both counter-increment loops (`ctr[15..12]`, `V[15..0]`), `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update`'s 3-block loop and NULL `provided_data`, `randombytes` chunking (`xlen > 15`) and `reseed_counter` all byte-identical over a sweep of lengths {0,1,15,16,17,48,63,64,65,257} and chunk sequences {0,1,15,16,17,31,32,33,…}.\n- **`randombytes` symbol ownership**: `translation/src/randombytes.rs` has **no** `#[no_mangle]` (only `pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn randombytes_urandom`, `randombytes.rs:90`), so the single exported `randombytes` comes from `rng.rs:413`. `nm -D --defined-only` on `cbuild/sha2-robust-192f/{libsphincs_core_det.so,libsha2.so}` vs `rbuild/sha2-robust-192f/libsphincs_core_det.so` gives an **exactly identical** symbol set (no C-only, no Rust-only). Correct.\n- **Differential sweeps that came out byte-identical** (4 configs: `sha2-robust-128s`, `haraka-simple-256f`, `blake-robust-192s`, `shake-simple-128f`): all ten address setters/copiers with random 32-bit/64-bit values and self-aliasing (`copy_subtree_addr(a,a)`), `chain_lengths`, `wots_pk_from_sig`, `wots_gen_leafx1` (incl. `wots_steps` values > 15 and `wots_sign_leaf` matching/not matching), `fors_gen_leafx1`, `fors_sign`, `fors_pk_from_sig`, `merkle_sign` (`idx_leaf` = 0, `~0`, random), `merkle_gen_root`, `compute_root` (`tree_height` 1–12 × random 32-bit `leaf_idx`/`idx_offset`), `treehash` (`tree_height` 0–6, in- and out-of-range `leaf_idx`)