{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_q3w6nc4jh2w3hoeuigkjf3ztbgepesyte7zb6zvyz3ygi7o24nua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four completion-gate conditions hold.\n\n## Result\n\n**60/60 Rust feature combinations pass** (48 distinct C configurations × the `shake256` alias), with 0 symbol-parity gaps, 0 failing Phase B rows, and 0 failing Phase C rows.\n\n### Phase A artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 309 lines, generated by `gen_symbols.sh`. Per-config `nm -D` parity table for all 48 configs + full per-backend symbol listing. **0/48 configs with missing symbols**; 0 unresolved non-libc undefined symbols in any of the 48 Rust `.so`s. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 8 runtime-rejection rows (4 in `sign.c`, 3 in `rng.c`, 1 unreachable OpenSSL `abort`), 22 boundary rows (B1–B22), 5 crash-equivalent rows (C1–C5), and the compile-time `#error` table. All 29 named tests exist and pass. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 3 build axes (48 configs) + 17 runtime axes + 41 rows, each `[x]`. All 41 named tests exist and pass. |\n\n### Symbols fixed (were absent from the Rust `.so`)\n`AES256_ECB`, `DRBG_ctx` (all 48 configs) and `cst` (blake's non-`static` `const u64 cst[16]`).\n\n### Real divergences found by the tests/audit and fixed in Rust\n1. `SPX_treehash` — auth-path slice was `tree_height*N`; C writes up to `(tree_height+1)*N`, so Rust aborted where C wrote (incl. `tree_height == 0`).\n2. `wots_gen_leafx1` — `wots_steps`/`wots_sig` were modelled as `Option`/inline array and **silently skipped** the access on NULL, i.e. returned a *different answer* than C's fault. Now raw pointers, dereferenced unconditionally.\n3. `seedexpander` — `ctx->buffer_pos > 16` (caller-owned state) made Rust panic-abort; C wraps `16 - buffer_pos`, reads adjacent struct bytes and returns `RNG_SUCCESS`. Now raw-pointer arithmetic off the struct base.\n4. `SPX_compute_root` — `tree_height == 0` panicked before mutating `addr`; C reads, mutates and hashes first.\n5. `crypto_sign`/`crypto_sign_open` — used `copy_from_slice` where C uses **`memmove`** (the in-place `sm`/`m` overlap idiom). Now `core::ptr::copy`.\n6. `thash` (shake, haraka) — fixed stack scratch aborted for `inblocks > max(WOTS_LEN, FORS_TREES)`; C uses unbounded VLAs. Heap fallback added (blake/sha2 already had one).\n7. `spx_ctx` layout — `state_seeded_512` was present unconditionally under `sha2`; C guards it with `#if SPX_SHA512`, so the struct was 72 bytes too large for `sha2-128*`. Now cfg-gated via a new `spx_big_hash`, and `build.rs`'s cfg precedence was realigned with `params.rs`/`context.rs`/`backend/mod.rs`.\n8. `SPX_treehash` NULL `gen_leaf` — now faults like C instead of a Rust panic.\n\nTwo authoritative C quirks are replicated, not \"fixed\": `hash_blake.c` passes **byte** counts to `blake*_update`, whose parameter is a **bit** count (so only `mlen/8` message bytes reach the digest), and `gen_message_random` writes the full 64-byte BLAKE-512 digest through a caller `R` pointer that only owns `SPX_N` bytes.\n\nHarness: `build_c_all.sh`, `build_rust_all.sh`, `symdiff.sh`, `gen_symbols.sh`, `run_all.sh`; `run_all.log` holds the final run. `c_src/` is unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":608,"cache_read_input_tokens":477308,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":608,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea246c20-3a08-49a0-aeed-8ef41fe5c703","uuid":"8c87a6bc-569d-4f8c-adbf-de1971ed4ebb","timestamp":"2026-09-02T16:16:42.173Z"}
